WEBVTT

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:03.110
Marie!

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.160
Stay away!

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.620
Wretched fool, forcing the truth
on me when I don't want to see it!

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.960
I was planning to disappear by myself.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.220
If you guys are here,
there's no point anymore!

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.720
Why do you have to disappear?

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:34.970
I am the same kind of being
as Kunino-Sagiri and Ameno-Sagiri.

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:38.810
I took those two out myself!
You don't have to...

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.060
No.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.070
It's because you took them out.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.360
The Sagiris and I...

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.950
It's not just our role to learn
what you humans desire.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:54.870
Our true role is to respond to
human desire and control the fog.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.370
Control the... fog?

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.040
Didn't you find it strange?

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:05.260
That fog never lifted for months on end,
yet it never spread outside the city.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:10.590
The Sagiris produce the fog,
and I absorb it.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.800
That's my job.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:18.600
Even after I'd lost my memory,
I was subconsciously carrying out that job.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:23.270
Are you saying that she'd
absorbed the fog? Marie?

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:27.610
That's right.
I'd absorbed it into my body.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:31.070
That fog that led humans astray!

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.790
Why do you think the fog
 lifted in your world?

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.620
Because you defeated
 Ameno-Sagiri? Wrong!

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.950
If anything, the defeat of Ameno-Sagiri

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:48.970
should have caused the torrents of fog
stored inside him to flow outward.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:55.970
But that didn't happen. In that case,
where did all that fog go?

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.310
Don't tell me.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.100
It all came flowing into me.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:05.860
Even as we speak,
the fog is roiling inside me.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:09.110
And now I feel like I'm about to go insane.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:16.870
If the fog inside me were to leak out,
the world will be covered in fog, and eventually...

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:22.830
And so I'm going to vanish
along with this Hollow Forest.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:26.960
That way, the world
will be saved. That's...

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:30.300
That's... my job.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.550
The true memories that I've recovered...

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:39.350
Oh, is that what this is about?

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:50.030
So long as you have the will to move on,

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:52.740
you shouldn't stop in your tracks.

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:58.240
Even if you've exhausted
the spirit to rise up again,

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:00.870
this bond of truth will
summon power for you.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.870
Over and over... Over and over...

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.380
We've got to go!

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.840
Marie's waiting!

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:34.950
What do you mean... "I hate you"?

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.950
You really stink at lying, Marie.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:03.480
I was your enemy all along!
There's no way I can be with you!

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:04.600
That's a load of crap!

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.690
Just stop, will you?

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:16.910
If your happiness is compromised,
then I won't know what I'm dying for!

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.280
You're only thinking of yourself!

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:27.000
Because I know.
That you're all busybodies.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:31.210
That's why I stole your memories
and kept you at a distance!

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:34.050
Who asked you to do such a thing?

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:37.130
You'd better drop it, Marie.

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:42.220
Your words are so hollow.
They're not resonating at all inside me!

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:49.730
Tell me what you're really thinking, Marie!

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.900
What's wrong with averting
my gaze from suffering?

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:58.740
I'd prefer a peaceful lie
over a painful truth!

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:02.160
Shut up! It's Marie's voice
that I want to hear!

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.410
Not yours!

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.580
Say it! Marie!

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:09.330
Shout it out! What you're
really feeling in your heart!

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.880
Moron... I hate you...

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:23.640
You suck... Saying that I don't care
if I die... of course that's a lie!

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:28.390
Why wouldn't I want to stay with you all longer?

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.440
I want to live...

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:33.610
Save me...

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.190
Yu...

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:38.650
Of course I will!

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:45.580
I can hear it, guys!
Marie-chan's voice!

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:51.460
Hey, I get it now! This is the place where
Marie-chan's soul showed up onscreen.

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:54.590
So here it is... Marie-chan's favorite...

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:58.630
Where they sell those rock-hard
beefsteaks - Souzai Daigaku!

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:07.770
I saw it, too!

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:09.850
Okina City, where we all went
shopping together!

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:12.600
The place where we created
our cherished memories!

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:17.440
That beach we went to!

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:18.980
Remember how pretty it was?

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:23.110
Going there with you was so much fun!

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:26.790
The fireworks, the quiz show,

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:29.250
You were there with us for all of it!

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:33.170
So how can we let you die alone now?
No way can we do that!

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:37.090
That concert we sang together in!

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:39.090
That's the best memory I have!

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:41.550
I won't let you say
that you don't want it!

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:44.680
Knowing the truth,
the pain it brings you...

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:46.640
I totally get it, okay?

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:49.390
So I'm not gonna let you be alone!

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.940
The truth is painful,
but you're not the only one!

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:57.110
Even if it is, you should
still go on living with us.

00:08:57.110 --> 00:08:58.650
You can go on living!

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:00.610
If you're with your friends!

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:04.820
Marie, your voice of truth...

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:07.030
It reached us.

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:08.910
So...!

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:14.460
All these myths...
I'm going to shatter them all!

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.800
Marie!

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:11.390
Yu!

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:18.690
Welcome home.

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:21.900
I'm home now...

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:54.600
Isn't that epic hug a little too long?

00:10:55.140 --> 00:11:00.730
No way. Letting go of you... standing on my own...
They're both impossible for me.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:02.440
Too tiring!

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:04.980
Hey!

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:08.150
I guess there weren't a whole lot of people
that you could rag on, Rise-chan.

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:09.860
That's mine, all right?

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:12.620
If you're gonna steal it, then you
need permission from my agency!

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:15.580
I mean, my sponsors aren't
going to let this go!

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:20.830
The earth is shaking from
our babies' red-hot sparks!

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:23.960
No time for that stuff!
What's going on?

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:26.460
This place is supposed to be my grave.

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:29.090
I don't need it if
I'm not gonna die,

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:30.800
so of course it's going up in smoke!

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:33.510
Hey, don't gimme that!
Tell us sooner!

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:35.770
Or else we're gonna go
up in smoke with it!

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:39.600
We're gonna die! We're
gonna kick the bucket!

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:42.560
Come on, head for the exit! Hurry!

00:11:56.830 --> 00:11:57.450
Marie?

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.400
Marie, what are you laughing about?

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:49.090
That was close. I thought
for sure our number was up.

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:52.300
Being alive is a wonderful thing, huh?

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:54.640
I'll drink to that!

00:12:56.390 --> 00:12:57.430
What?

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:01.270
Just now, the Hollow Forest
got wiped out completely.

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:04.690
Because there's no reason
for it to exist anymore.

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:05.900
Yeah, I guess.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:07.900
Bye-bye, grave!

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:11.280
Um... Listen...

00:13:11.820 --> 00:13:14.990
Thanks for rescuing me.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:16.280
Also...

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:18.280
I'm sorry...

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.250
Wh-What? What's up with that reaction?

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:26.380
Hey, did you just say "sorry"?

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:28.800
Yes, she did! She just came out and said it.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:29.750
Huh?

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:32.300
Well, hey, it's not like you.

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:33.470
That kind of thing...

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:36.890
Huh? H-H-H-How stupid is that?

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:42.680
Never mind! I-I-I-I take it back!
Forget it, okay?

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:44.770
Oh, boy!

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:47.190
She's back to being her old self again.

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:49.480
But this is more like Marie-chan.

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.860
True. That's the Marie we know!

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:53.070
Now there's no question.

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:53.650
Nope.

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:56.610
What's up with that?
Hey, revise that statement!

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:02.200
Come on, listen to me!
Anyway, what's up with you guys?

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:05.870
Look how hurt you got,
coming to my rescue!

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:10.800
Nothing good came of it
for you guys! I just don't get you!

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.800
Well, you might not get us, but...

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:14.880
Right?

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:17.970
Oh... Hey, look!
It's totally sunny outside!

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:19.930
Hey, you're right!

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:25.100
Oh, man, my back's totally sore!
Hey, wanna go grab something to eat?

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:27.770
Good idea! Needless to say,
it's your treat, Hanamura!

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:31.110
Huh? Why are you
saying that like it's a given?

00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:36.490
H-Hey!

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:42.160
Why are you guys...

00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:45.580
But you know, don't you? The truth is...

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:51.000
I have no idea...

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:54.920
Wow! Look! The snow's sparkling!

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:57.380
It is! It's so pretty!

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:00.930
What's wrong?

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:03.060
When you guys showed up,

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:07.600
I thought I heard someone
else's voice coming out of me.

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:08.730
That was...

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:10.060
A voice? Whose?

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:14.030
I don't know. But it was
a familiar voice...

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:20.490
It was the same voice I heard
when you defeated Ameno-Sagiri,

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:22.620
and the fog started flowing into me.

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:24.700
Huh? Or maybe not.

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:27.500
Actually, it could've been my own voice.

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:31.420
Oh, well, never mind.
The fog's gone anyway.

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:33.590
I must have misheard it.
Forget I said that!

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:38.050
Hey, my bad! I was aiming for Yu...

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:39.800
Hey, bull's-eye!

00:15:40.050 --> 00:15:41.930
You're It next, Marie-chan!

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:43.810
No, it's not that kind of
game, you know.

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:46.310
Senpai, come over here and join us!

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:49.190
Now that it's sunny out,
and there's all this snow,

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:51.350
don't you want to do this kind of thing?

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:53.610
Do you know what
a snowball fight is, Marie-chan?

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:56.110
Wait, I guess you can
learn while you're playing!

00:15:56.110 --> 00:15:58.240
Hey, how should we split up into teams?

00:15:58.240 --> 00:15:59.570
Huh?

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:00.700
What's that?

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:02.700
Huh? Whoa! What the heck?

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:07.120
Whoaaaaa! What's up with that?

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:10.670
You're supposed to throw these,
right? The snow. Am I wrong?

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:11.830
That's perfect.

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:13.170
What's so perfect?

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:15.300
Okay, let's split up into teams.

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:16.340
Seconded!

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:17.590
Good idea.

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:20.550
It's the Marie-chan Team vs. the Junes Team!

00:16:20.550 --> 00:16:22.340
This is no team!

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:24.390
Hey, no hard feelings, Yosuke.

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:25.760
Jeez! You, too?

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:27.520
All right! Ready...

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:29.020
Start!

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:32.100
Sink!

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:36.520
That's not what you say
during a snowball fight!

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:42.910
Hey, that was a rout!

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:46.200
It's ten years too soon
to be taking us on.

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:49.830
Well, you do have to feel
a little sorry for him.

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:54.630
But today's hero is Marie-chan,
wouldn't you say?

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:57.130
Hey, Snowball Queen!

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:03.050
You've got the wrong
gender. Not hero - heroine.

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:06.890
Wow! Marie-chan, your skin is gorgeous!

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:10.680
I'm more envious of Naoto-kun...

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:11.600
Huh? Of what?

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:13.020
They really are amazing...

00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:15.190
You're right! They're totally amazing...

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:17.650
H-Hey! Please don't stare at me like that!

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:18.530
Well?

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:20.690
I can't see with all this steam.

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:23.410
Oh, crap. Huh? Where's Yu?

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:25.070
What's up?

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:27.160
Don't go building stuff in the bath!

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:30.200
Kanji, can't you go higher?

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:34.170
Huh? Look, you, you're using someone's
head. Don't gimme that attitude!

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:37.960
Is this as high as your head will go, Kanji?

00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:40.090
I guess you're just a loser, then, huh?

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:41.590
Damn you! Teddie!

00:17:41.590 --> 00:17:43.550
Whoa! Dumbass!

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:54.640
You guys...

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:56.350
You really haven't learned
your lesson, have you?

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:59.400
H-Hold up, you guys! That
murderous intent is overpowering!

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:01.400
At least let us explain!

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:09.830
What are you doing?

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.710
Uh, actually, this is...

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:17.330
H-Hold up! Calm down!

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:18.710
Don't shock us!

00:18:18.710 --> 00:18:20.840
You guys...

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:23.340
I hate your guts!

00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:34.430
Big Bro!

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:38.860
Big Bro, do you know what day it is today?

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:42.030
Beats me, what day is it again?

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:45.860
Huh? There are things
that even you don't know?

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:49.570
Oh, there are tons.
You sure are a know-it-all.

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:52.040
Will you tell me what day it is?

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:56.620
Okay! Sure! Um...
you see, today is...

00:18:58.120 --> 00:18:59.380
Valentine's Day!

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:05.170
You see, the big girls showed me
how to make homemade chocolate!

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:08.930
Big Sis Chie told me to put some bacon in,

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:11.050
because there's no one
who doesn't like meat.

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:12.140
N-Nanako...

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:17.120
Rise-chan said that personality was everything,
so it should be really hot or sweet.

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:20.700
Since you're a grownup, Big Bro,
I thought you'd like it to be bitter,

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.820
so I added some peppers and aojiru!

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:24.280
Nanako... Listen...

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:28.950
Big Sis Yukiko told me that adding
some fish would give it a deeper flavor.

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:33.450
So I added some fish sausage
and Dad's salty fish guts!

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:35.160
Nanako... Um...

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:38.920
You're not gonna eat it?
It's gonna melt...

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:47.420
Listen, Big Bro...

00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:50.340
Thank you for everything.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:52.180
I love you!

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:54.760
Nanako... Big Bro...

00:19:56.810 --> 00:19:58.690
...loves you, too!

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:08.700
I'm home! What's wrong?
You look pretty awful.

00:20:09.110 --> 00:20:12.910
Oh, it's nothing.
You're early today, Uncle.

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:15.580
Well, I'm still not up to
pushing myself too hard...

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:20.210
Is that right? Well, of course.
You should take care of yourself...

00:20:20.870 --> 00:20:24.380
Hey! Where you going?
You're staggering...

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:26.210
I have an appointment.

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:31.130
You're late.

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:34.220
Sorry. Something came up.

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:43.270
Oh, um.... The others clued me in.

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:49.150
What day it is today. Girls are supposed to...
um... tell whoever's dear to them

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:50.950
"I... I..."

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:53.820
"Th-Thank you" - this is the day
they're supposed to tell them that, right?

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:55.780
Yes, that's what I heard.

00:20:57.540 --> 00:20:59.040
Here...

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:00.040
What's this?

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:02.500
Y-You know what it is! Chocolate.

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:03.790
Chocolate?!

00:21:03.790 --> 00:21:08.340
Wh-What's the matter?
You'd better eat it now or it'll melt.

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:09.200
If it melts...

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:10.070
It'll escape...

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:10.820
Escape?!

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:15.640
There's no outlet in that room,
so it might not taste too good.

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:18.930
But I did work hard to make it, so...

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:22.770
If you eat it... I-I'd be happy...

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:28.270
Marie...

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:32.360
Thank you.

00:21:38.370 --> 00:21:42.080
I never thought you'd
eat it all up. You're amazing.

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:43.790
Or are you a moron?

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:47.130
It's like something's
squirming around inside..

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:58.810
I was able to come back, huh?

00:21:59.180 --> 00:22:01.140
Don't ever go away again.

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:04.600
Who are you to talk?
You're leaving yourself.

00:22:05.100 --> 00:22:08.310
That's so unfair... dumbass... jerk...

00:22:11.860 --> 00:22:13.320
That's true...

00:22:17.070 --> 00:22:22.330
If only I could stay here... Forever...

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:05.320
Write a wish?

00:24:05.320 --> 00:24:06.430
A wish, huh?

00:24:06.430 --> 00:24:09.630
They wish for a world enshrouded in fog!

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:11.630
You can't fall here!

00:24:11.790 --> 00:24:12.730
I...

00:24:12.830 --> 00:24:14.740
My wish is...
